# What the vendors state

- DeepSeek (https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing): model id
  deepseek-flash, version DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017; "Vision ✓" for Flash and
  "Not supported" for V4-Pro. The vision guide lists OpenAI Chat image_url,
  Anthropic image blocks (base64/url/file) and Responses input_image, with
  "Images are supported in user messages only".
- Alibaba Model Studio DeepSeek FAQ: "deepseek-v4.1-flash and
  deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 support text and image input and text-only output".
  The page does not state which request format carries the image.
- Ollama deepseek-v4.1-flash:1017-cloud: tags list "Text, Image input".

# Verified code facts before the change

- Claude/Anthropic wire preserves image blocks end to end:
  protocols/chat_projection.py openai_multimodal_content converts them for a
  chat wire, and the native Anthropic path forwards the body unchanged.
- Ollama's native chat wire did NOT: anthropic_messages_to_ollama ran every
  user block through content_to_text, which ignores image blocks, so an
  attached image disappeared without any error.
- The Codex catalog is built from a bundled template
  (codex debug models --bundled: all 10 templates declare ["text","image"]),
  so every routed model inherited image input — including deepseek-v4-pro,
  which the provider documents as text only.

# Change

- protocols/chat_projection.py: ollama_image_payloads() collects inline
  base64 image blocks, and the user message carries them as Ollama's
  "images" list. A remote URL cannot be forwarded on this wire and is left
  out; an image-only message is kept.
- providers/alibaba.py: deepseek-v4.1-flash (and the -1017 snapshot) returns
  a Codex catalog with input_modalities ["text","image"];
  other DeepSeek models on this adapter state ["text"] so a previously
  applied image catalog cannot leak onto a text-only model.

# Verification

- evidence/codex-catalog-check.txt: real Codex catalog generation on this
  machine (codex debug models --bundled) yields
  deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 -> ['text','image'],
  deepseek-v4.1-flash -> ['text','image'],
  deepseek-v4-pro -> ['text'], qwen3.8-max -> ['text','image'].
- tests/test_ollama_image_input.py: inline image reaches the Ollama message,
  image-only message kept, URL/empty source add nothing, text-only history
  unchanged.
- tests/test_alibaba_provider.py: AlibabaDeepSeekVisionTests covers all three
  adapters and both model ids, plus the text-only reset.
- evidence/focused-tests.txt: 239 exact-file tests OK. Ruff and diff
  whitespace checks passed.

# Not established

Whether Alibaba's Anthropic-compatible endpoint forwards images for this model
(their docs state model support and endpoint support separately). No model
endpoint was called, so this is a wire/catalog fix, not a live image round
trip. Claude Code on this session received the user's pasted screenshots, so
the Anthropic path already worked here.
